==Icelandic==

===Etymology===
From {{suffix|kenna|gloss1=to teach|ari|gloss2=suffix used to create agent nouns from verbs|lang=is}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{IPA|/ˈcʰɛnːaːrɪ/|lang=is}}
*: {{rhymes|ɛnːaːrɪ|lang=is}}

===Noun===
{{is-noun|m|kennara|kennarar}}

# a [[teacher]]
#: ''Hún er góður '''kennari'''.''
#:: She is a good '''teacher'''.
#: ''Jónas er undarlegur '''kennari''', en samt skemmtilegur.'
#:: Mister Jónas is a strange '''teacher''', but fun nevertheless.

====Usage notes====
* Like most occupational terms, ''kennari'', although grammatically masculine, may be used for either sex. The term {{m|is|kennslukona}} (literally “teaching woman”) may also be used to refer to a female teacher specifically.

